1. CURRENT OBJECTIVE
==================================================

Today our A2UI dashboard is effectively rendered using a fixed dashboard/grid arrangement, approximately a 2 × 2 layout.

I want to evolve this into a dynamic A2UI dashboard where:

- The backend/agent generates A2UI widgets incrementally.
- Widgets can arrive one by one through SSE / AG-UI.
- The frontend renders each widget immediately.
- The dashboard automatically arranges widgets based on semantic layout metadata.
- Different widgets can have different widths.
- Different widgets can have different heights.
- The layout should automatically adapt as new widgets arrive.
- The layout must be responsive.
- We use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- The backend/agent must NOT generate Tailwind CSS classes.
- The frontend should own the actual CSS/Tailwind implementation.
- A2UI should describe semantic layout information.
- We should avoid hardcoding a 2 × 2 dashboard.
- We should preserve our existing A2UI architecture rather than replacing it.

The target concept is:

Agent
